# inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded Design

Date: 2026-06-27

Status: Implemented first pass in the UnrealMCP editor bridge after explicit
Ieta/Tivret proceed request. Keep future changes editor-only and read-only.

Scope: editor-only, read-only animation asset metadata inventory for
`UAnimSequenceBase`, `UAnimSequence`, and `UAnimMontage`. Runtime/gameplay code
is out of scope.

## Purpose

`inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded` is a narrow UnrealMCP bridge
command for requests that need source animation asset metadata:

- notifies and notify states;
- animation curves and optional bounded curve keys;
- authored sync markers;
- Montage sections, slots, and segments;
- branching-point evidence derived from notifies, not private Montage caches;
- asset, skeleton, preview mesh, asset metadata, and user-data class summaries.

The command exists to prevent failed loops where an agent tries broad Unreal
Python reflection against version-sensitive animation internals.

## Ieta Review

Request class: read notify, curve, sync marker, Montage section, slot, segment,
or branching-point metadata from an animation asset.

Existing routes checked:

- `inspect_anim_instance_runtime_state` reads live AnimInstance montage and
  curve state, not source asset metadata.
- `inspect_anim_graph_protected_topology` and
  `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings` read AnimBP graph topology/settings, not
  animation asset metadata.
- `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose` proves runtime pose contribution, not
  authored notifies, sync markers, or Montage layout.

Why existing routes are insufficient: they answer runtime or graph questions,
but they do not safely inventory source animation asset metadata.

Asset mutation boundary: read-only. The command must not save, compile, tick,
evaluate a world, call Notify handlers, edit packages, or mark packages dirty.

Implemented command: `inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded`.

Default safety guard: support only loaded or loadable `UAnimationAsset`
subclasses, require bounded result sizes, and return `unsupported_class` for
non-animation assets.

Approval state: user approved Ieta/Tivret to proceed. This command is limited to
the UnrealMCP editor bridge and does not add runtime/gameplay code.

## UE 5.6 API Anchors

Use installed UE 5.6 headers as local truth:

| Need | UE 5.6 anchor | Safe access rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Asset identity, skeleton, preview mesh | `Animation/AnimationAsset.h` `UAnimationAsset` | Use public `GetSkeleton()`, `GetPreviewMesh()`, `GetMetaData()`, and `GetAssetUserDataArray()`. |
| Sequence length and rate | `Animation/AnimSequenceBase.h` `UAnimSequenceBase` | Use `GetPlayLength()`, `RateScale`, `bLoop`, `GetNumberOfSampledKeys()`, and `GetSamplingFrameRate()`. |
| Notifies | `Animation/AnimSequenceBase.h` and `Animation/AnimTypes.h` | Read `UAnimSequenceBase::Notifies`; summarize `FAnimNotifyEvent` fields without dispatching notifies. |
| Notify tracks | `Animation/AnimSequenceBase.h` | Read `AnimNotifyTracks` under editor-only data when available; otherwise use `TrackIndex`. |
| Curves | `Animation/AnimData/IAnimationDataModel.h` and `Animation/AnimCurveTypes.h` | Prefer `GetDataModel()->GetFloatCurves()`, `GetTransformCurves()`, and `GetAttributes()` in editor; fallback to `GetCurveData()` summaries. |
| Sequence sync markers | `Animation/AnimSequence.h` and `Animation/AnimTypes.h` | Read public `UAnimSequence::AuthoredSyncMarkers`; include `UniqueMarkerNames` when available. |
| Montage marker data | `Animation/AnimMontage.h` | Read public `MarkerData.AuthoredSyncMarkers`, `SyncGroup`, and `SyncSlotIndex`. |
| Montage sections | `Animation/AnimMontage.h` | Use `GetNumSections()`, `GetSectionName()`, `GetSectionStartAndEndTime()`, `GetSectionLength()`, and `GetAnimCompositeSection()`. |
| Montage slots and segments | `Animation/AnimMontage.h` and `Animation/AnimCompositeBase.h` | Read public `SlotAnimTracks`; summarize `FAnimSegment` references, start/end, play rate, and loop count. |
| Branching points | `Animation/AnimTypes.h` and `Animation/AnimMontage.h` | Derive from `FAnimNotifyEvent::IsBranchingPoint()` and public notify indices. Do not depend on private `BranchingPointMarkers`. |

## Command Schema

Proposed input fields:

| Field | Type | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `asset_path` | string | required | Long package path or object path for an animation asset. |
| `include_notifies` | bool | `true` | Include notify and notify-state summaries. |
| `include_notify_details` | bool | `true` | Include class names, filters, trigger chance, and branching flag. |
| `include_curves` | bool | `true` | Include curve names, types, flags, and counts. |
| `include_curve_keys` | bool | `false` | Include bounded key samples only when explicitly requested. |
| `include_sync_markers` | bool | `true` | Include sequence or Montage marker data. |
| `include_montage_sections` | bool | `true` | Applies to `UAnimMontage`. |
| `include_montage_slots` | bool | `true` | Applies to `UAnimMontage`. |
| `include_metadata` | bool | `false` | Include asset metadata/user-data class names only. |
| `max_notifies` | int | `256` | Clamp to implementation maximum. |
| `max_curves` | int | `256` | Clamp to implementation maximum. |
| `max_curve_keys_per_curve` | int | `0` | Ignored unless `include_curve_keys=true`. |
| `max_markers` | int | `256` | Clamp to implementation maximum. |
| `max_sections` | int | `128` | Clamp to implementation maximum. |
| `max_slots` | int | `64` | Clamp to implementation maximum. |
| `max_segments_per_slot` | int | `256` | Clamp to implementation maximum. |
| `require_supported_class` | bool | `true` | Return a structured unsupported result instead of best-effort dumping. |

Suggested hard clamps:

- `max_notifies <= 1024`
- `max_curves <= 1024`
- `max_curve_keys_per_curve <= 256`
- `max_markers <= 1024`
- `max_sections <= 256`
- `max_slots <= 128`
- `max_segments_per_slot <= 512`

## Response Schema

Top-level result:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "command": "inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded",
  "read_only": true,
  "asset_modified": false,
  "saves_assets": false,
  "asset": {},
  "sequence": {},
  "montage": {},
  "notifies": [],
  "curves": [],
  "sync_markers": [],
  "metadata": {},
  "limits": {},
  "truncated": {},
  "warnings": [],
  "errors": [],
  "unavailable_fields": []
}
```

`asset` fields:

- `path`, `name`, `class`, `package`;
- `skeleton_path`, `preview_mesh_path`;
- `play_length`, `rate_scale`, `loop`;
- `supported_class`, `is_sequence_base`, `is_sequence`, `is_montage`.

`sequence` fields:

- `sampled_keys`, `sampling_frame_rate`, `has_root_motion`;
- `authored_sync_marker_count`, `unique_marker_names`;
- `data_model_valid`, `data_model_frames`, `data_model_keys`,
  `data_model_frame_rate`.

`notifies` item fields:

- `index`, `name`, `event_name`, `type`;
- `notify_class`, `notify_state_class`;
- `trigger_time`, `end_trigger_time`, `duration`, `track_index`,
  `track_name`;
- `trigger_weight_threshold`, `trigger_chance`, `filter_type`,
  `filter_lod`, `can_be_filtered`, `trigger_on_dedicated_server`,
  `trigger_on_follower`;
- `montage_tick_type`, `is_branching_point`,
  `converted_from_branching_point`.

`curves` item fields:

- `name`, `curve_kind`, `flags`, `key_count`;
- `source`, one of `data_model_float`, `data_model_transform`,
  `data_model_attribute`, `runtime_curve_data`, or `fallback`;
- optional bounded `keys` when `include_curve_keys=true`.

`sync_markers` item fields:

- `index`, `name`, `time`, `track_index`, `track_name`, `source`.

`montage` fields:

- `sync_group`, `sync_slot_index`, `blend_in_time`, `blend_out_time`,
  `blend_out_trigger_time`, `enable_auto_blend_out`;
- `sections`: section name, start, end, length, next section, metadata class
  names;
- `slots`: slot name, track length, bounded segments;
- `branching_point_state_notify_indices`;
- `branching_points`: notify-derived branching point summaries.

## Forbidden Patterns

Do not use these in implementation:

- ad hoc Python crawling of `AnimSequence`, `AnimMontage`, or private notify
  internals;
- direct access to private Montage caches such as `BranchingPointMarkers`;
- calling `Notify`, `NotifyBegin`, `NotifyTick`, or `NotifyEnd`;
- ticking an AnimInstance, world, actor, or SkeletalMeshComponent;
- writing to `RawCurveData`, `Notifies`, `CompositeSections`, or
  `SlotAnimTracks`;
- sorting, refreshing, rebuilding, compiling, saving, or marking the asset
  dirty;
- returning unbounded curve keys, notify objects, UObject property dumps, or
  serialized binary data;
- treating runtime curve values as authored curve metadata.

Reason: these patterns either mutate assets, invoke gameplay/editor side
effects, depend on private version-sensitive caches, or create huge unstable
responses.

## Verification Plan

For docs-only changes:

```powershell
git diff --check
```

For a future implementation:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python -m py_compile unreal_mcp_server.py tools\node_tools.py
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat' MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development -Project="$Project" -WaitMutex
```

Editor smoke verification after implementation should:

- read one `UAnimSequence` and one `UAnimMontage`;
- confirm `read_only=true`, `asset_modified=false`, `saves_assets=false`;
- compare dirty package count before and after the command;
- confirm notifies, curves, markers, sections, and slots obey requested limits;
- confirm unsupported assets return structured `unsupported_class` errors;
- confirm `include_curve_keys=false` never returns full key arrays.

## Tivret Maintenance Notes

Implement nothing from this document unless the active request explicitly moves
from design to command implementation. When approved, keep the implementation
editor-only and read-only:

- target files: likely
  `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/Commands/UnrealMCPBlueprintNodeCommands.cpp`,
  matching public declaration header, `Python/unreal_mcp_server.py`,
  `Python/tools/node_tools.py`, and `Docs/Tools/node_tools.md`;
- do not touch runtime/gameplay modules;
- do not mutate assets or generate Unreal assets;
- use UE 5.6 public accessors and editor DataModel APIs first;
- return explicit warnings for unavailable private or editor-only fields;
- rollback boundary: remove the new command, wrapper, docs entry, and tests
  only; do not revert unrelated docs or user changes.
